    "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-concept-purpose-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Concept | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| Epoch size | Total target admissions for one epoch. |\n| Worker pool size | Number of worker slots the run loop tries to keep active. |\n| Candidate window | Number of ranked board candidates scanned to satisfy admission. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-worker-pool-size-is-the-36": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-worker-pool-size-is-the-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker pool size is the claim/process target, not the raw compiler parallelism\ntarget. Worker processes can be active while their expensive validation or\ntool calls are queued behind per-epoch tool slots. The active epoch still owns a\nfixed admitted target set; the slot queues only smooth local CPU/build pressure\ninside the already-claimed work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-there-are-three-hot-path-37": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-there-are-three-hot-path-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "There are three hot-path capacity controls:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-run-director-loop-control-owns-38": {
      "id": "b-10-run-director-loop-control-owns-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Control | Owns |\n| --- | --- |\n| Worker pool | Number of live worker claims/processes. |\n| Epoch ready queue | Number of admitted, unclaimed targets kept available to feed worker slots. |\n| Tool/build slots | Number of concurrent compile-heavy validation and Pi tool operations allowed across worker worktrees in an epoch. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
